## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a beginner PCA pipeline in a cross-tenant setting with latency constraints and interpret loadings for cohort definitions. Emphasizes data cleaning, scaling, component retention strategy, and practical mapping from components to business actions.

## Key Concepts
- PCA basics: imputation, scaling, centering
- Global vs per-tenant PCA; explained variance threshold
- Loadings interpretation; cohort definition
- Latency considerations: batch vs streaming; incremental options

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating preprocessing and PCA call
function buildPCA(data) {
  const imputed = imputeMeanPerFeature(data);
  const scaled = scaleToUnitVariance(imputed);
  // assume PCA is available and returns components/loadings
  const pca = new PCA(scaled, {nComponents: 6});
  return pca.loadings;
}
```

```javascript
// Example interpretation
const top = pcaLoadings[0];
console.log(top); // { sessions_per_week: 0.68, content_views: 0.52, ... }
```

